// Scala's inlining-adjacent tools are by-name parameters and specialisation.
// A by-name argument is evaluated only if used, and HotSpot inlines a simple
// by-name expression at the call site - so the branch costs nothing if untaken:
@inline def branch(useHeavy: Boolean, heavy: => Any, light: => Any): Any =
  if (useHeavy) heavy else light        // `heavy` is evaluated only if useHeavy

// On Scala.js there is no JIT (no inlining); on Scala Native it uses LLVM.
// Do not carry a HotSpot-inlining assumption to those targets.
